OL,3,GNEWSAFrom inoperable cancer to free of
OL,4,Athe disease
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former nurse has been declared cancer
OL,7,Ffree after receiving a pioneering
OL,8,Fchemotherapy treatment for inoperable
OL,9,Fovarian cancer.
OL,11,FCaroline Ainslee, 60, from Southampton,
OL,12,Fwas diagnosed with stage-four ovarian
OL,13,Fcancer in March after the disease
OL,14,Fspread to her liver, lungs and other
OL,15,Fparts of her body.
OL,17,FHowever, she responded well to initial
OL,18,Ftreatment and became one of the first
OL,19,Fovarian cancer patients at University
OL,20,FHospital Southampton to receive
OL,21,Fhyperthermic intraperitoneal
OL,22,Fchemotherapy (HIPEC).
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
